these are my options for lua_ls, im also using nvim-lspconfig plugin if that makes any difference

```lua
    on_init = function(client)
        if client.workspace_folders then
            local path = client.workspace_folders[1] and client.workspace_folders[1].name
            if path and (vim.loop.fs_stat(path .. "/.luarc.json") or vim.loop.fs_stat(path .. "/.luarc.jsonc")) then
                return
            end
        end

        client.config.settings.Lua = vim.tbl_deep_extend("force", client.config.settings.Lua, {
            runtime = {
                version = "LuaJIT",
            },
            workspace = {
                checkThirdParty = false,
                library = {
                    vim.env.VIMRUNTIME,
                    "${3rd}/luv/library",
                },
            },
        })
    end,
    settings = {
        Lua = {
            doc = {
                privateName = { "^_" },
            },
            hint = {
                enable = true,
                setType = false,
                paramType = true,
                paramName = "Disable",
                semicolon = "Disable",
                arrayIndex = "Disable",
            },
            completion = {
                callSnippet = "Replace",
            },
        },
        telemetry = {
            enable = false,
        },
    },
```

Here is a gif of it happening, as you can see, when I delete the current file im in, the lsp progress component in my statusline shows up, the notification is the file the lsp attaches to and also the lspinfo shows an additional lua_ls with no root directory

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/99261805-bf7b-4ff7-8d7c-1fa9bc385036)

Also just one more thing, is it possible to have an option passed in for mini files that allows it to be not closed when another window is opened/focused, right now mini files closes when I open vim.ui.select or vim.ui.input and causes them to close as well, which I have some use cases for with lsp rename. Thanks!
